<div style="text-align:center; font-size:28px; font-weight:bold;">
    NumPy Arrays and Reshaping
</div>
<br>
<div style="font-size:18px;">

# Question 1
Create a one-dimensional NumPy array containing gene expression values `[2.1, 4.2, 1.5, 3.8, 2.9]`. Print the array and its shape.
<br></br>

# Question 2
Using `np.full()`, create a 2x3 array filled with the value 
**0.5**. Print the array.
<br></br>

# Question 3
Generate a sequence using `np.arange()` from 0 to 14 with step size 2, then use smart reshaping with -1 to create a matrix with 4 columns. Print both arrays.
<br></br>

# Question 4
Create a 2x2x2 three-dimensional array using `np.ones()`. Print both the array and its shape.
<br></br>

# Question 5
Create an array with numbers 1-12, then reshape it into a 3x4 matrix. Print both the original array and the reshaped matrix.
<br></br>
